The seed corpus's CT leaves for revokt's spec §9.2 (revision 45: at least 100 000 CT leaves of the index issuers, the
issuers of the fixture generation's CRLite filters), in two sets: the log sample (logs/) and the crt.sh top-up
(crtsh/). Each set is 16 shards <0-f>.tsv.gz by the sha256's first hex digit: sha256 of the DER, source, index or
crt.sh id, entry type (0 x509, 1 precert), base64 DER.

logs/: the random log sample of revokt-corpus v4 (ct-seed/leaves/ there) without CT test traffic.
  The sample was collected from 2026-10-25T23:56:38Z to 2026-10-26T00:22:38Z by tools/ct-seed/collect.py:
    python3 -I tools/ct-seed/collect.py --ct-logs ct-seed/ct-logs.json --seed 20261026 --tiles 5 --batches 8 --out ct-seed
  110043 distinct certificates as logged (final certificates of x509 entries, precertificates of precert entries)
  out of 118528 entries read, from five random full data tiles of each static-ct-api log and eight random 256-entry
  get-entries batches of each RFC 6962 log, paged until complete, among the 81 CRLite-enrolled logs; 80 logs
  answered, and one did not (Let's Encrypt Oak2026h2, get-sth). sample.json records each log's checkpoint or signed
  tree head as read, the tiles read and the index ranges read; its distinct_leaves is the sample's before the drop.
  tools/ct-seed/drop-test-issuers.py then copied the shards line for line without the leaves whose issuer Name (DER,
  by SHA-256) is a CT test issuer, which log operators and monitors use to test logs and no root program trusts:
    python3 -I tools/ct-seed/drop-test-issuers.py --leaves <v4 checkout>/ct-seed/leaves --out ct-seed/logs
    dropped 35447: C=GB, ST=London, O=Google UK Ltd., OU=Certificate Transparency, CN=Merge Delay Intermediate 1
    dropped  7407: O=Geomys, CN=CT Uptime Test Root
    dropped  1598: CN=DigiCert CT Monitor, C=US, ST=UT, L=Lehi City, O=DigiCert, Inc.
    dropped     2: C=CN, O=TrustAsia Technologies, Inc., CN=TrustAsia DV TLS ECC Test CA G4
