limits: log entries are not checked against an inclusion proof, and a log that serves fewer entries than its tree
  size would show a shorter index range in sample.json. crt.sh's certificates are checked against their issuers'
  keys only, not against any log. crt.sh's ca.last_not_after showed no update after 2026-10-24 (seen on 2026-10-29),
  so CAs were chosen by key, not by recorded activity. The shards are written with Python's gzip at level 9 with no
  name or time (Python 3.14.7, zlib 1.2.12; crtsh.json's versions); another zlib changes their bytes, not their
  content.
licence: the leaves of logs/ are CT log entries, public records; those of crtsh/ are certificates crt.sh holds (its
  precertificates and final certificates, not checked against a log), and crt.sh states no data licence; they are
  CA-published, unmodified. ct-logs.json is Mozilla Remote Settings data.
